<main><section class="ei-hero"><div class="shell ei-split"><div><p class="kicker">ETF operations</p><h1>See the operational handoffs behind ETF outcomes.</h1><p class="lead">ETF creation and redemption activities can involve issuers, authorized participants, custodians, administrators and multiple technology environments. Execution Intelligence helps investigate where work waits, repeats or diverges.</p><div class="ei-actions"><a class="btn btn-light" href="mailto:connect@revivetoday.com?subject=Banking%20Execution%20Intelligence">Discuss your workflow</a><a class="btn btn-outline-light" href="/workflows">Explore workflows</a></div></div><img alt="Execution Intelligence visualization" decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="/images/banking/large-global-banks-execution-patterns-800.webp"/></div></section><section class="band"><div class="shell"><div class="head"><p class="kicker">Illustrative workflow</p><h2>From instruction to reconciliation</h2><p>A representative operational sequence; actual responsibilities and systems vary by fund structure, participants and operating model.</p></div><div class="ei-steps"><div><span>01</span><strong>Creation / redemption instruction</strong></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Validation and approvals</strong></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Basket and asset coordination</strong></div><div><span>04</span><strong>Settlement and custody handoffs</strong></div><div><span>05</span><strong>Reconciliation and exception resolution</strong></div></div></div></section><section class="band"><div class="shell"><div class="head"><p class="kicker">Execution questions</p><h2>What becomes visible?</h2><p>The opportunity is to understand the operating process, not to execute trades or replace ETF infrastructure.</p></div><div class="ei-cards"><article class="ei-card"><h3>Where do delays originate?</h3><p>Identify the preceding steps and handoffs associated with late or exception-prone cases.</p></article><article class="ei-card"><h3>Which exceptions repeat?</h3><p>Distinguish normal operating variation from recurring rework and control loops.</p></article><article class="ei-card"><h3>How do participants interact?</h3><p>Reconstruct a case across linked records and teams where reliable identifiers exist.</p></article><article class="ei-card"><h3>Did a change help?</h3><p>Compare execution patterns before and after process or technology changes.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="band band-paper"><div class="shell ei-feature"><div class="ei-placeholder"><span>NEW VISUAL PLACEHOLDER</span><strong>ETF execution map</strong><small>Approved illustration or RE-ViVE workflow screenshot to be created later</small></div><div><h2>Built on the same platform.</h2><p>ETF operations are a proposed application of RE-ViVE’s process-agnostic execution mapping. This page does not imply an existing ETF customer deployment.</p><a href="/platform">Explore the platform →</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="ei-footer"><div class="shell"><img alt="RE-ViVE" decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="/images/revive-logo-inverse-240.webp"/><p>Understand how work actually executes.</p><p><a href="/">Banking Home</a> · <a href="/workflows">Banking</a> · <a href="/platform">Platform</a> · <a href="https://re-vive.com/">Corporate Website</a></p><small>© 2026 RE-ViVE. Product and use-case information. Outcomes depend on each institution’s data and environment.</small></div></footer>
</Layout>
